.TH QFW_MPI_SMOKE.SH 1 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Examples"
.SH NAME
qfw_mpi_smoke.sh \- validate the QFw application-owned MPI service path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_mpi_smoke.sh [--verbose]
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw_mpi_smoke.sh
starts the specialized
.B mpi-smoke
service from the installed example manifest, launches one application task,
and verifies a call through
.BR api_mpi_smoke .
The wrapper owns and tears down its directory and service runtime.
.PP
This test has its own service manifest and task-placement contract. It does not
accept backend or site-service options and is intentionally separate from
.BR qfw_run_all.sh (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --verbose
Enable shell tracing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QFW_MPI_SMOKE_NP
MPI rank count. The default is 2.
.TP
.B QFW_MPI_SMOKE_TIMEOUT
Directory lookup and service connection timeout in seconds. The default is 40.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the smoke test in a one-node allocation:
.EX
salloc --nodes=1 --ntasks=1 --time=00:15:00
source /opt/openqse/qfw/current/bin/qfw-activate \e
  --venv /opt/openqse/qfw/venv
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_mpi_smoke.sh
qfw-deactivate
.EE
.PP
Run it after a heterogeneous allocation has been granted:
.EX
export QFW_RUN_BASE_DIR=/shared/openqse/qfw/application-runs
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_mpi_smoke.sh --verbose
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw_run_all.sh (1),
.BR qfw-examples (7),
.BR qfw-srun (1),
.BR qfw-service-lifecycle (7)
